01559"} "24 from 18 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147477"} "Bobby Finke"] " (USA) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/124275"} "Gregorio Paltrinieri"] " (ITA) had won gold in this event in 2020 and 2016 and were still the favorites, along with Ireland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/143924"} "Daniel Wiffen"] ", who had won the 800 freestyle five days before this final."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Finke is known for his fast finishes, but in the final he took the lead on the first lap and never relinquished it. Splitting ahead of world record pace throughout, he finished in 14:30.67 to break the world record of 14:31.02 set by China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/112216"} "Sun Yang"] " in winning the 2012 Olympic gold."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Finke held throughout, as Paltrinieri was second at every checkpoint and took the silver medal, almost four seconds behind Finke. Wiffen likewise moved into third at 300 metres and held that position to the finish for the bronze medal. Fifth place went to Türkiye’s 16-year-old " [:a {:href "/athletes/154773"} "Kuzey Tunçelli"] ", who was second for 300 metres and finished in a world junior record of 14:41.22."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Finke became the fourth swimmer to defend the 1,500 freestyle gold medal, after American " [:a {:href "/athletes/51283"} "Mike Burton"] " in 1968-1972, and Australians " [:a {:href "/athletes/45268"} "Kieren Perkins"] " in 1992-1996 and " [:a {:href "/athletes/93263"} "Grant Hackett"] " in 2000-2004. Soviet swimmer " [:a {:href "/athletes/50888"} "Vladimir Salnikov"] " also won the event twice, in 1980 and 1988."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147477"} "Bobby Finke"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https:/